From: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: net2280: NET2282: give back a torn down DMA
 queue with -ESHUTDOWN

nuke() and usb_reset_228x() stop the DMA of an endpoint through
abort_dma(), whose scan_dma_completions() gives back, with status 0,
every request whose descriptor reads as done. From within
usb_ep_disable() this can be a transfer done by the engine but not yet
seen by the irq handler; on a NET2282 it seemingly also is the OUT
transfer that the abort itself stopped: every unbind of a CDC NCM
gadget with the OUT endpoint on DMA is followed by
"net2280_queue: error=-108", i.e. a request that rx_complete() got back
with status 0 and resubmitted after the reset.

u_ether does not expect such a completion inside usb_ep_disable(). In
gether_disconnect(), port_usb is already NULL: rx_submit() returns
-ENOTCONN without putting the request back on rx_reqs, so it is never
freed ("dma_pool_destroy requests busy" when net2280 is removed after
a gadget with OUT DMA, never after one with OUT PIO). In eth_stop(),
which holds dev->lock across usb_ep_disable(), rx_complete() takes
dev->lock again to unwrap an NCM transfer.

On the NET2282 only, retire nothing as completed when a queue is torn
down: abort or stop the engine as before, and let nuke() give every
request back with -ESHUTDOWN, as the PIO paths do. Data that the
engine moved for a request not yet given back is dropped, as data
still in the fifo is with PIO. The register writes are unchanged.
NET2280 and USB338x paths, and abort_dma() everywhere else (dequeue,
halt), are unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Radeon24 <Radeon24@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/net2280.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/net2280.c
@@ -1240,6 +1240,33 @@
 	scan_dma_completions(ep);
 }
 
+/* abort_dma() for a queue being torn down (endpoint disabled, controller
+ * reset): on the NET2282, retire nothing as completed, so that nuke()
+ * gives every request back with -ESHUTDOWN, as the PIO paths do.  The
+ * scan of abort_dma() may give back an OUT request with status 0 from
+ * within usb_ep_disable(): a transfer done by the engine but not seen
+ * by the irq handler yet, and on the NET2282 seemingly also the transfer
+ * that the abort itself stopped (a "net2280_queue: error=-108" follows
+ * every unbind with OUT DMA).  u_ether then resubmits that request
+ * where it does not expect any completion but -ESHUTDOWN: from
+ * gether_disconnect(), once port_usb is NULL, rx_submit() drops it (the
+ * request and its dma descriptor leak: "dma_pool_destroy requests busy"
+ * at rmmod), and from eth_stop(), which holds dev->lock, rx_complete()
+ * takes dev->lock again to unwrap an NCM transfer.
+ */
+static void abort_dma_teardown(struct net2280_ep *ep)
+{
+	if ((ep->dev->quirks & (PLX_LEGACY | PLX_2280)) != PLX_LEGACY) {
+		abort_dma(ep);
+		return;
+	}
+	if (likely(!list_empty(&ep->queue))) {
+		writel(BIT(DMA_ABORT), &ep->dma->dmastat);
+		spin_stop_dma(ep->dma);
+	} else
+		stop_dma(ep->dma);
+}
+
 /* dequeue ALL requests */
 static void nuke(struct net2280_ep *ep)
 {
@@ -1248,7 +1275,7 @@
 	/* called with spinlock held */
 	ep->stopped = 1;
 	if (ep->dma)
-		abort_dma(ep);
+		abort_dma_teardown(ep);
 	while (!list_empty(&ep->queue)) {
 		req = list_entry(ep->queue.next,
 				struct net2280_request,
@@ -2101,7 +2128,7 @@
 	for (tmp = 0; tmp < 4; tmp++) {
 		struct net2280_ep       *ep = &dev->ep[tmp + 1];
 		if (ep->dma)
-			abort_dma(ep);
+			abort_dma_teardown(ep);
 	}
 
 	writel(~0, &dev->regs->irqstat0),
